summary:
- topic: Superintendent Search and Board Workshops
  text: The board announced upcoming dates for the superintendent search, including
    an executive session to determine a base salary and a public presentation by Zeal
    on the leadership profile. Other workshops include non-biased hiring training
    for the board and several budget workshops.
- topic: Community School Model Expansion
  text: Dr. Rebecca Stern and Liana Popkin presented the successful Community School
    Model at South Portland Middle School, highlighting its positive impact on absenteeism,
    family engagement, and academic achievement. The board voted to approve the expansion
    of this strategy across the district, starting with the high school, to leverage
    state funding and community partnerships.
- topic: FY27 Budget Development Feedback
  text: Dr. Johanna Prince shared themes from recent budget forums, indicating strong
    community value for education despite challenges like declining enrollment and
    rising costs. Stakeholders emphasized student needs, equity, transparency, and
    long-term financial sustainability, with many data requests focusing on elementary
    school reconfiguration.
- topic: Pre-Kindergarten and Child Development Services (CDS) Updates
  text: Dr. Johanna Prince provided updates on the pre-K lottery for the next school
    year, emphasizing a new mandatory screening process for all applicants. South
    Portland is joining Cohort 3 of the CDS transition, taking on responsibility for
    4-year-olds with special education needs, and exploring partnerships with United
    for Childcare and Headstart.
- topic: Athletic Complex Update
  text: Mike Nalli and Todd Livingston provided an update on the athletic complex
    project, detailing plans for an eight-lane track, natural grass field, new lights,
    and permanent restrooms. The timeline for construction is projected for April
    2027, with potential delays depending on state permitting for impervious surface
    area.
- topic: FY25 Audit Findings and Financial Management
  text: Abigail Chen, Director of Finance, reported on the FY25 audit, noting a material
    finding related to reconciliation procedures and a significant deficiency with
    federal costs. She also highlighted the ongoing nutrition fund deficit and emphasized
    the multi-year effort required to stabilize the district's financial house due
    to past instability in the business manager role.
- topic: Policy Reviews and Cell Phone Policy Discussion
  text: The Policy Committee presented first reads for Policy BEDH (Public Participation
    at Board Meetings) and an addendum to Policy BCA-E (Ethics Policy) regarding Rules
    of Decorum. Discussion also touched upon the cell phone policy, with the board
    deciding to defer a full review until later in the year due to current priorities.
- topic: Support for City Council Immigration Resolve
  text: 'The board unanimously voted to endorse the South Portland City Council''s
    Resolve #5-25/26 concerning federal immigration enforcement and community safety.
    Board members expressed strong support for the immigrant community and acknowledged
    the significant impact recent events have had on students and families.'
- topic: Elementary School Reconfiguration Proposal
  text: The board voted to request a formal proposal from the superintendent regarding
    the benefits and impact of elementary school reconfiguration. Board members emphasized
    the need for extensive community input and data to inform this significant decision,
    acknowledging the strong community sentiment surrounding neighborhood schools
    and budget realities.
