      are being formalized as part of the ethics policy.'
  - seconds: 5993
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: The committee also discussed the cell phone policy, noting a potential state
      mandate for a bell-to-bell prohibition. While it's a critical issue, the committee
      decided to defer a full review due to the board's current heavy workload. The
      high school is already working on its own procedure, and the issue will be revisited
      later, likely after a new superintendent is hired.
  - seconds: 6066
    speaker: Eleni Richardson
    text: I was not aware that the policy committee had decided to table the cell
      phone policy discussion. I'd like to understand the process for this decision
      and propose that we identify June as the time for the policy committee to discuss
      it, as it's important not to delay it too long.
  - seconds: 6120
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: The decision to defer was made after consultation with the interim superintendent,
      determining that this is not the time to take on that issue. We can discuss
      prioritizing it at a policy committee meeting, and if two of the three committee
      members agree, it can be moved forward for board action. The superintendent
      search and other policies are currently higher priorities.
  - seconds: 6183
    speaker: Claire Holman
    text: I hope we can address the cell phone policy soon. It will require significant
      work to figure out systems, potential purchases, and costs. Teachers and staff
      are important stakeholders, and it wouldn't be fair to delay it too long. I'm
      glad if we can get to it in the spring, as another school year without addressing
      it would be unacceptable, regardless of state action.
